The routine lgt-s computes the common logarithm of a whole number from 1 to 999, by pseudo-division, three-digit
remainder.

Input: x from 1 to 999. Result: 1000 log10 x rounded, from 0 to 3000, laid out as a table of logarithms lays it
out: the characteristic times 1000 plus the three-digit mantissa. STO keeps the mantissa and SFT 03 leaves the
characteristic; log10 200 gives 2301.

Call: load x into the accumulator and JMP 22. It returns with the result in the accumulator.
Cells 22-98 (77 cells). It writes cell 99 and, of its own cells, 69-71, 98; nothing else.
Cost: at most 265 instructions a call, 139.4 on average over the domain, counted from the calling JMP to the
return jump. Worst error: 1 in the last digit (thousandths) against the correctly rounded value, at x = 9; 241 of
the 999 inputs are off.
To move the routine down by d cells, subtract d from every address in its instructions that points into
cells 22-98; addresses 00 and 99 stay as they are. It holds no address bases.

